        {
          "id": 1875777942,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Sorry, what I meant was:\nIf we rely only on one flag ie.,\"IS_6GHZ\" alone, it may not be backward compatible. \n\nHope the captures below, justify the use of 2 flags.\n\n1. If we use only IS_6GHZ flag, an older version sniffer device may be setting the corresponding bit to 0, even for 6GHz traffic, because it was a reserved bit till now.\n\nThus, new version wireshark could wrongly identify the 6GHz frame from old version sniffer device, as belonging to 5GHz or 2.4GHz band.\n\nI simulated this error at wireshark side, by relying only on just one flag \"IS_6GHz\". Please see below how a 6GHz beacon's frequency could get computed incorrectly:\n\n![Single_Flag_6GHz_Frame_Interpreted_as_2.4GHz](/uploads/8cc0cabc4fbf7f351cd76566c6e5a437/Single_Flag_6GHz_Frame_Interpreted_as_2.4GHz.png)\n\n\n2. The \"6GHZ_BAND_VALID\" flag safeguards against this, and makes the change backward compatible. \n\nIf \"6GHZ_BAND_VALID\" is not set, Peekremote V0 dissector will read the \"IS_6GHZ\" flag, and it will not attempt to determine frequency. \n\nPlease see below decoding of the same frame **using changes in this commit**.\n\n![Two_Flags_6GHz_Frame_Frequency_Not_computed](/uploads/474609649046135ddc800d1cfa7e6b3f/Two_Flags_6GHz_Frame_Frequency_Not_computed.png)\n\n\n3. Finally, with a sniffer device that support the new fields, the frequency gets correctly computed as shown below, **using the changes in this commit**:\n\n 6GHz Beacon\n\n![Two_Flags_6GHz_Frame_Frequency_Correctly_Computed](/uploads/9e3c810d7a06e0bb97ef060629d61e8c/Two_Flags_6GHz_Frame_Frequency_Correctly_Computed.png)\n\n 2.4 GHz Beacon\n\n![Two_Flags_2GHz_Frame_Frequency_Correctly_Computed](/uploads/a2e673f90e51ea0bc8fd33dcf84852b6/Two_Flags_2GHz_Frame_Frequency_Correctly_Computed.png)",
          "author": {
            "id": 19290085,
            "username": "kripa-v",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "kripa",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
